; roster-sleeper.fk — a kernel that opens its live page and takes a roster slot as it starts, works a
; moment so its page reads hot rows, then rests three seconds, so the census
; (form/form-stdlib/kernel-roster.bml) can read it while it lives. Run with a number after the cell
; (./fkwu observe/tests/roster-sleeper.fk 7), the census still names the cell. Started by
; form/form-stdlib/tests/host-process-band.fk, by observe/tests/orphan-maker.fk and by the witnesses in
; receipts/2026-09-11-the-roster-speaks.md.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
(do
    (defn rs-spin (n acc) (if (le n 0) acc (rs-spin (sub n 1) (add acc 1))))
    (let w (rs-spin 5000 0))
    (let s (host_sleep_ms 3000))
    0)
